{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0FuaW1hdGlvbi8yMDExLS0yMDIwL1N3b3JkJTIwQXJ0JTIwT25saW5lJTIwVGhlJTIwTW92aWUlMjBPcmRpbmFsJTIwU2NhbGUlMjAlMjgyMDE3JTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Sword Art Online The Movie Ordinal Scale","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/2szdEK0Mr0RG0nWGFVTseNQHbnP.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/yFZG86Zvdy6JuIlMW9eHxlVkct5.jpg","description":"In 2026, a new machine called the Augma is developed to compete against the NerveGear and its successor, the Amusphere. A next-gen wearable device, the Augma doesn't have a full-dive function like its predecessors. Instead, it uses Augmented Reality to get players into the game. It is safe, user-friendly and lets users play while they are conscious, making it an instant hit on the market. The most popular game on the system is “Ordinal Scale” an ARMMORPG developed exclusively for the Augma. Asuna and the gang have already been playing OS for a while, by the time Kirito decides to join them. They’re about to find out that Ordinal Scale isn’t all fun and games…\n\nRated PG-13 · Released 18 Feb 2017 · Japan · Language: Japanese · 119 min\nStudio: A-1 Pictures, Aniplex, ASCII Media Works\n\nOn your server — Audio: Japanese, Hindi (from file names)","releaseInfo":"2017","genres":["Animation","Action","Adventure","Fantasy","Animation"],"imdbRating":"7.7","runtime":"119 min","cast":["Yoshitsugu Matsuoka","Haruka Tomatsu","Kanae Itou","Ayana Taketatsu","Rina Hidaka","Ayahi Takagaki","Miyuki Sawashiro","Hiroaki Hirata"],"director":["Tomohiko Ito"],"released":"2017-02-18T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"It's just a game... Or so I thought—","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Tomohiko Ito","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/GyFpjtodiP19QlMue8Yu41N3gG.jpg"},{"name":"Yoshitsugu Matsuoka","character":"Kazuto Kirigaya / Kirito (voice)","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/ugDwdWEXnmv43jcbnfAi4XwiQ8C.jpg"},{"name":"Haruka Tomatsu","character":"Asuna